# Factory layering

REST and RPC are **adapters**. They parse transport input, call the business layer, and map results to status codes or RPC envelopes. They must not contain workflow CRUD or run rules.

## Where logic lives

- **Business** (`src/business`): list/get/create/update/delete/soft-delete workflows, `showDeleted`, start run, get run. Returns domain data or throws `FactoryError`.
- **REST** (`src/http`): HTTP parse, `createFactoryService`, JSON status/body. Keep the existing curl/JSON API working.
- **RPC** (`src/rpc`): RPC parse, the **same** business functions, `{ ok, data | error }`. No REST fetch as a backdoor.

## UI

The Next.js UI talks to the business layer **over RPC only** (server actions wrapping `src/rpc`). Do not `fetch` `/workflows` or other REST routes as the primary path.

Do not put business rules in Next.js route handlers, `app/api/**`, or HTTP `create-server.ts` beyond transport mapping.

## Conversion

JSON → domain conversion has one import site: `src/business/definition.ts`, which calls `validateWorkflowDefinition`. Persist submitted JSON. GET/list/UI return the stored document as-is. Do not add a JSON↔Node codec.
